From: LilSmokeOS developers
Subject: [PATCH] controller: avoid an unaligned word store into Joybus replies

PIF replies are byte-packed. The standard controller reply starts three
bytes into the command buffer, so a uint32_t pointer cast causes SIGBUS
on MIPS32r2. Preserve the exact existing byte order with memcpy.
Observed under MIPS74Kf/musl with the project's SI polling fixture.

--- a/mupen64plus-core/src/device/controllers/game_controller.c
+++ b/mupen64plus-core/src/device/controllers/game_controller.c
@@ -223,7 +223,7 @@
     case JCMD_CONTROLLER_READ: {
         JOYBUS_CHECK_COMMAND_FORMAT(1, 4)
 
-        *((uint32_t*)(rx_buf)) = input_;
+        memcpy(rx_buf, &input_, sizeof(input_));
 #ifdef COMPARE_CORE
         CoreCompareDataSync(4, rx_buf);
 #endif
